{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/937572-statting-up-mentors-retainers","id":937572,"title":"Statting Up Mentors / Retainers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-26T06:41:13-07:00","id":937572,"title":"Statting Up Mentors / Retainers","content":"I know there are hard n' fast rules in the book on rolling dice for Mentors / Retainers, but assuming you wanted to create a more detailed stat-sheet for these specific NPCs, I was wondering what house-rules / design choices people could use to create Mentors / Retainers according to their 'levels'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T08:04:56-07:00","id":937605,"title":"","content":"Back in 1e, my group had the following housrule regarding Retainers:<br /> <br /> * Standard human character; Attributes only<br /> ** Standard human character; Attributes and Skill only OR sub-template with Attributes only<br /> *** Standard human character;OR sub-template with Attributes and Skills only; OR template with Attributes only<br /> **** Standard human character +10 XP; OR standard sub-template; OR template with Attributes and Skills only<br /> ***** Standard human character +20 XP; OR sub-template +10 XP; OR standard template<br /> <i>In all cases, sub-templates and templates get whatever Advantages come standard.</i><br /> <br /> Mentors were usually just a narrative thing, but when we did stat them up, I used these guidelines:<br /> <br /> * Standard character +20 XP<br /> ** Standard cahracter +30 XP<br /> *** Standard character +50 XP<br /> **** Standard character +90 XP<br /> ***** Standard character +140 XP<br /> If the Mentor was a sub-template character, I'd give an extra 10 XP, for a human I'd add 20 XP.<br /> <br /> Granted, these guidelines were used with 1e's multiplicative XP costs, so it'd need some conversion to work with 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T08:05:11-07:00","id":937606,"title":"","content":"In our sessions we use to create new character sheets for the Retainers. Assuming that there is a 3-dot Retainer, no ability, skill, merit or anything goes beyond 3 dots. Then we create the new character (Retainer) as a fresh character. With Mentors we never used that cause we keep them in a more RP side that not gonna affect the game drastically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11988-montgomery-crobes","name":"Montgomery Crobes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T09:35:17-07:00","id":937643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>inkpenavenger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/937572-statting-up-mentors-retainers?p=937605#post937605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in 1e, my group had the following housrule regarding Retainers:<br /> <br /> * Standard human character; Attributes only<br /> ** Standard human character; Attributes and Skill only OR sub-template with Attributes only<br /> *** Standard human character;OR sub-template with Attributes and Skills only; OR template with Attributes only<br /> **** Standard human character +10 XP; OR standard sub-template; OR template with Attributes and Skills only<br /> ***** Standard human character +20 XP; OR sub-template +10 XP; OR standard template<br /> <i>In all cases, sub-templates and templates get whatever Advantages come standard.</i><br /> <br /> Mentors were usually just a narrative thing, but when we did stat them up, I used these guidelines:<br /> <br /> * Standard character +20 XP<br /> ** Standard cahracter +30 XP<br /> *** Standard character +50 XP<br /> **** Standard character +90 XP<br /> ***** Standard character +140 XP<br /> If the Mentor was a sub-template character, I'd give an extra 10 XP, for a human I'd add 20 XP.<br /> <br /> Granted, these guidelines were used with 1e's multiplicative XP costs, so it'd need some conversion to work with 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dividing by 5 should do it, the way the math works out, 1 beat in 2e is more or less equivalent to 1 experience in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T07:55:16-07:00","id":942711,"title":"","content":"Given how low rating characters are said to be very bad, I use this system to stat them up:<br /> For Mortals/Ghouls <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px; width: 917px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">Retainer Dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">Attributes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">Skills</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">Specialties</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">Merits</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">Disciplines if ghoul</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">3/3/2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">5/3/2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">1 (physical)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">4/3/3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">8/5/3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">1 (physical) + 1 (any)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">5/4/3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">11/7/4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">1 (physical) + 2 (any)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">6/4/4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">14/9/5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">2 (physical) + 2 (any)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">7/5/4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">17/11/6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">11</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">2 (physical) + 3 (any)</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T08:11:15-07:00","id":942716,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity. When Every human starts at 5/4/3 and 11/7/4 with 7 merits. How do you justify giving them less than what every human starts with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T08:15:42-07:00","id":942721,"title":"","content":"Not every human starts out with that. Every player character starts out with that. Going of the Retainer rules themselves - dot 1 retainer has two dice in some rolls and 1 dice in the rest of them. Starting character states cannot have such bad rolls all over the place <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> Along with that, we have a shitload of stat blocks for all sorts of characters which are lower than the normal thing. <br /> <br /> And going even further, have you checked how many dots a starting character actually get's? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm yet to meet a real world person who would need that many dots to be represented correctly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T08:27:24-07:00","id":942729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/937572-statting-up-mentors-retainers?p=942721#post942721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not every human starts out with that. Every player character starts out with that. Going of the Retainer rules themselves - dot 1 retainer has two dice in some rolls and 1 dice in the rest of them. Starting character states cannot have such bad rolls all over the place <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Along with that, we have a shitload of stat blocks for all sorts of characters which are lower than the normal thing.<br /> <br /> And going even further, have you checked how many dots a starting character actually get's? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm yet to meet a real world person who would need that many dots to be represented correctly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good point. Yes. Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T09:19:21-07:00","id":942749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/937572-statting-up-mentors-retainers?p=942721#post942721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not every human starts out with that. Every player character starts out with that. Going of the Retainer rules themselves - dot 1 retainer has two dice in some rolls and 1 dice in the rest of them. Starting character states cannot have such bad rolls all over the place <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Along with that, we have a shitload of stat blocks for all sorts of characters which are lower than the normal thing.<br /> <br /> And going even further, have you checked how many dots a starting character actually get's? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm yet to meet a real world person who would need that many dots to be represented correctly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Go to a famished village in Africa and see if everyone got all those merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T20:13:05-07:00","id":944092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/937572-statting-up-mentors-retainers?p=942711#post942711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how low rating characters are said to be very bad, I use this system to stat them up:<br /> For Mortals/Ghouls <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px; width: 917px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">Retainer Dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">Attributes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">Skills</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">Specialties</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">Merits</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">Disciplines if ghoul</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">3/3/2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">5/3/2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">1 (physical)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">4/3/3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">8/5/3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">1 (physical) + 1 (any)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">5/4/3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">11/7/4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">1 (physical) + 2 (any)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">6/4/4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">14/9/5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">2 (physical) + 2 (any)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">7/5/4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">17/11/6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">11</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 2px\">2 (physical) + 3 (any)</td> </tr> </table></div></div> </div> </div> </div>This is excellent. How would you do Mentors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T02:51:45-07:00","id":944207,"title":"","content":"Mentors are very different and it cannot be so clear cut. Mainly, because Mentor is not under such control of the character as is a Retainer.<br /> For example, what Mentor 1 can represent? A fairly incompetent friend in finances, who ghelps with Academics, Politics and Resources. But it can also represent an ancient vampire, who is simply unwilling to share too much with you, only giving you small part of the information he has himself (so still just Mentor 1).<br /> <br /> I keep the Mentor dots as they are pretty much. When a player requests information from a mentor (i'm yet to have someone ask for intervening..). Similarly to Allies, I assign a successes rating, of how much one needs for the Mentor to know it. So sometimes the request is out of scope for the mentor. Sometimes, he only knows a part of what's being asked of (in my specific games, sometimes my mentors get asked about devotions, so only a part of what they are is revealed).Etc.<br /> <br /> Anyways, it all comes down to the simple fact, that Mentor dots don't represent just the skill of the Mentor, but also his willingness to share information. <br /> <br /> One of my players had a BP 8 Circle of the Crone Hierophant as a Mentor. His knowledge is great, but a lot of times he would withhold information, in favor of his pupil learning on his own. I also had a Knight of the Invictus as a mentor, he would almost never withhold information, but simply he did not have such a knowledge base to work with. <br /> <br /> The Knight was a 2 dot Mentor while the Hierophant only 1 dot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}